Rules:
  [K1] Use `val` by default, `var` only when needed.
  [K2] Use null-safe operators (`?.`, `?:`).
  [K3] Use `when` expression instead of `switch`.
  [K4] Use string templates.
  [K5] Use data classes for DTOs.
  [K6] Use extension functions sparingly.
  [K7] Use coroutines for async.
  [K8] Use sealed classes for state.

Pros:
  - Concise syntax
  - Null safety
  - Java interop

Cons:
  - Compile times
  - Tooling maturity
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Java (mature)
  - Flutter (cross-platform)
  - Swift (Apple ecosystem)

State: +

